Z||000000||FieroHarry||05-27-2001||05:55 PM||||Hi everybody,<BR>Yesterday it rained again, I finally got good weather today and decided to change out my sun roof seal. At 264K miles it was trashed hard and so is the metal retaining frame work thats rivited in place.<BR>My question is this:<BR>The back edge of the sunroof bows quite a bit and is not touching the seal correctly by the latching mech..<BR>I would like to place a piece of hard rubber under the latch to make it clamp just a tiny bit harder (but not enough to break the glass)to help my seal be a little tighter.<BR>How does the latch bracket (inside) come off?<BR>Has anyone ever tried this?<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||9
Z||000001||tgowens||05-27-2001||06:05 PM||||Harry, remove the latch cover held by one phillips head screw. Underneath you will see the latch is held by two 11mm nots. Remove those and the latch will fall into your lap.......you may want to scribe the position the latch is in before removing it as you will notice that the latch is adjustable and can be moved front to rear. You will also notice a flat black plastic "spacer" on the top side of the latch.<P>I have "shimmed" many of them to aid in the closing of the sunroof.......adding the thickness of the spacer will make all the difference in the world.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroHarry||05-27-2001||06:18 PM||||tgowens u da man!<BR>Thanks a bazillion <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
